message: "If you use Pad-Lattice, please cite the software."
title: "Pad-Lattice: A Visual Protocol for AI Agent Control on Physical and Virtual Surfaces"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rueda
    given-names: Manuel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9280-058X"
version: 0.2.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23777302"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mrueda/pad-lattice"
url: "https://mrueda.github.io/pad-lattice/"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Pad-Lattice turns physical controllers and virtual pads on phones,
  tablets, and computers into synchronized human-in-the-loop control surfaces
  for monitoring and directing multiple AI agents through a shared tactile
  visual language.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - agent supervision
  - human-in-the-loop
  - human-agent interaction
  - MIDI controllers
  - Elgato Stream Deck
  - Novation Launchpad
  - multi-agent systems
  - control surfaces
  - visual protocol
  - visual language
  - tangible user interfaces
